          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਬਸੰਤ (basant) is a semi-tatsama: Sanskrit vasanta, \"spring season\", borrowed after the old sound changes had run their course and then lightly reshaped (CDIAL 11439). Punjabi has b- for the v-; CDIAL lists no Punjabi form."
            }
