        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਪਤਝੜ (patjhaṛ) is built from two inherited words: pat, \"leaf\", as in Punjabi patt, from Sanskrit pattra (CDIAL 7733), and jhaṛ, from jhaṛṇā, \"to fall off\", which CDIAL lists under a reconstructed jhaṭati, \"falls\" (CDIAL 5328). Autumn is \"leaf-fall\"."
            }
          ]
        },
